  "runner_up_case": "ADVERSE is the honest runner-up because all three verdict-deciding questions (Q10 regulator sanction, Q11 criminal conviction/charge, Q12 major civil judgment) are still open, and the probes made so far are poorly matched to a small UK private company. court_records searches US CourtListener, which almost never indexes UK High Court or County Court judgments against an SME, so it provides near-zero coverage for Q12. The three news searches returned sources but no evidence item was extracted for any verdict-deciding question, so it is unknown whether those hits concerned company 08893883 or namesakes (e.g., overseas 'Option Energy' entities). No UK primary enforcement source was queried at all: not the HSE public register of prosecutions and enforcement notices, not the FCA Register or Warning List, not Environment Agency or Trading Standards/CMA records, and not The Gazette for insolvency or compulsory strike-off notices. The subject is an energy-services firm (youroption.co.uk, Steyning) — a sector with recurring HSE gas/electrical-safety prosecutions, consumer-law enforcement, and energy-contract mis-selling litigation, each of which would be material. Companies House 'Active' status answers only Q4 (not currently insolvent); it does not exclude a past administration, a pending strike-off, a criminal charge, or a regulator ban, and the profile page was quoted selectively (previous names, filing history and charges were never examined). On this record NO_ADVERSE is an absence-of-evidence conclusion, not an affirmative finding, and a single HSE prosecution or Gazette notice would flip it to ADVERSE.",
  "would_flip_it": [
    "An HSE prosecution, conviction, or safety enforcement notice against Option Energy Solutions Ltd (company 08893883) — e.g., unsafe gas or electrical work — which is both a criminal conviction/charge (Q11) and regulator enforcement (Q10).",
    "An FCA warning or final notice, entry on the FCA Warning List, or a CMA/Trading Standards enforcement action (consumer-protection injunction or formal undertakings) naming the company — regulator sanction under Q10.",
    "A Gazette notice for company 08893883: administration or liquidation appointment, CVA, or first Gazette notice for compulsory strike-off (past or pending), which would overturn the Q4 'Active' reading.",
    "A reported UK court judgment (BAILII or trade press) finding fraud or awarding damages of £500,000 or more against the company, e.g., an energy mis-selling or hidden-commission claim — major civil judgment under Q12.",
    "Companies House filing-history evidence contradicting the clean profile: a previous company name under which adverse events occurred, a registration/mortgage charge indicating large contested debt, or overdue accounts/confirmation statement alongside strike-off action.",
    "Verification that any of the unextracted hits from the earlier news_search and court_records steps actually concerns company 08893883 (not a namesake) and contains a material adverse fact."
  ]
}
